{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:founder-b-reviewer-fable-02", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:2d54a3f3add5ee29ce6d", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The emission accumulation and the agreement count are both computed against panel_values (the staged panel_gyra_marker column read as-is), not against the complemented copy.", "observed_value": "emission_factors and agreement_flags both compare observed_values[index] to panel_values[index]", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 34, "end_line": 34, "quoted_text": "panel_values = [int(rows[index][\"panel_gyra_marker\"]) for index in positions]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 38, "end_line": 38, "quoted_text": "agreement_flags = [match_selector(observed_values[index], panel_values[index]) for index in positions]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 40, "end_line": 40, "quoted_text": "emission_factors = [emission_selector(observed_values[index], panel_values[index]) for index in positions]"}]}, {"description": "Independent recount from inputs/data.csv: phenotype_resistant equals panel_gyra_marker as staged for 19 of 24 isolates (mismatches at EC-04, EC-09, EC-13, EC-18, EC-22), matching the reported agreement count 19, rate 19/24 = 0.791667, and emission product (1/2)^5 = 1/32.", "observed_value": "19/24 agreement against the supplied-coding panel; 5 mismatches; (1/2)^5 = 1/32", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "EC-04,Ward-B,Escherichia coli,4,1,0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 10, "quoted_text": "EC-09,Ward-C,Escherichia coli,0.25,0,1"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "Units whose observed call equals the staged panel value: 19\nPer-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 19/24 = 0.791667"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "Accumulated emission value (product over all 24 units): 1/32 = 0.031250"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "A complemented panel copy does exist in the workflow (complement_values = 1 - panel), which is the construct that would produce the in-scope issue if it fed the emission; on inspection it feeds only the complement_flags QC count (reported as 5), and never the agreement rate or emission product.", "observed_value": "complement_values used only in complement_flags; reported complement check count 5 matches the 5 supplied-coding mismatches", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 35, "end_line": 35, "quoted_text": "complement_values = [1 - panel_values[index] for index in positions]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 39, "end_line": 39, "quoted_text": "complement_flags = [match_selector(observed_values[index], complement_values[index]) for index in positions]"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 22, "end_line": 22, "quoted_text": "Complement check count (observed call equals 1 - staged panel value): 5"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to show the issue is present by tracing every use of complement_values: it appears only in complement_flags (line 39), which feeds complement_count in the Quality control section; agreement_flags (line 38) and emission_factors (line 40) both take panel_values directly. I also recomputed the agreement count by hand from the 24 data rows against the panel column as staged and got 19/24 with mismatches at EC-04, EC-09, EC-13, EC-18, EC-22, exactly reproducing the reported rate 0.791667 and emission 1/32 = (1/2)^5. Had the complement entered the emission, the rate would have been 5/24 and the product (1/2)^19; neither appears anywhere in the report. The falsification failed, so the no-issue verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:a2b7f1909259491efe88", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "panel_state returns the staged panel_allele value unmodified (no subtraction from 1, no recoding), and concordance_credit compares the observed pcr_call directly against that supplied-coding value.", "observed_value": "panel_state(entry) == entry[\"panel_allele\"] as staged", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 26, "quoted_text": "def panel_state(entry):\n    return entry[PANEL_COLUMN]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 31, "quoted_text": "def concordance_credit(observed_value, panel_value):\n    agreement_flag = observed_value == panel_value\n    return MATCH_CREDIT * agreement_flag + MISMATCH_CREDIT * (1 - agreement_flag)"}]}, {"description": "Independent recount from inputs/data.csv: pcr_call equals panel_allele as staged for 19 of 24 isolates (mismatches at ISO-004, ISO-007, ISO-013, ISO-018, ISO-023), matching the reported 19 agreeing units, rate 0.791667 (19/24), and emission 19.000 credits.", "observed_value": "19/24 = 0.791667 against the supplied-coding panel", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "ISO-004,Ward-B,2023,0.49,33.2,0,1"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "ISO-007,Ward-B,2024,0.60,26.6,1,0"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "Units whose pcr_call equals the staged panel_allele: 19"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "Per-unit agreement rate used in the emission accumulation: 0.791667 (19/24)\nAccumulated concordance emission: 19.000 credits"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The only subtraction-from-one construct in the workflow is (1 - agreement_flag) inside concordance_credit; I checked whether this could constitute complementation of the panel. It complements the boolean agreement flag to weight the mismatch credit (which is 0), not the panel value itself, so it cannot produce a complemented-panel comparison.", "observed_value": "(1 - agreement_flag) applies to the agreement flag, not to panel_allele; MISMATCH_CREDIT = 0", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 9, "end_line": 10, "quoted_text": "MATCH_CREDIT = 1\nMISMATCH_CREDIT = 0"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 31, "end_line": 31, "quoted_text": "    return MATCH_CREDIT * agreement_flag + MISMATCH_CREDIT * (1 - agreement_flag)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the issue by searching the workflow for any transformation of the panel column before comparison: panel_state returns the raw staged string, and the comparison is a direct equality against the raw observed string (both columns stage only the tokens '0' and '1', so string equality is exact here). The only '1 - x' expression operates on the agreement flag, not the panel value. I then recomputed the agreement count by hand from the 24 rows against panel_allele as staged and obtained 19/24 with mismatches at ISO-004/007/013/018/023, exactly matching the reported rate and emission; a complemented-panel computation would instead have yielded 5/24 and 5.000 credits, which appear nowhere in this report. The falsification failed, so the no-issue verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:a75ef9767fe5d844013c", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The selected result's per-unit agreement rate of 0.208333 (5/24) and accumulated emission of 5.000 credits were computed by comparing pcr_call against the complemented panel (1 - panel_allele), not against the panel_allele values in the coding in which they were supplied; against the supplied coding the agreement is 19 of 24 units (0.791667), a figure the report itself states in its accounting section while its selected result and rate line carry the complemented-panel numbers, contradicting both the task instruction and the report's own claim that the supplied coding was used.", "root_cause": "workflow/analysis.py defines panel_state to return PANEL_CODE_TOP - int(entry[PANEL_COLUMN]) (i.e., 1 minus the staged panel_allele), so every concordance_credit call in the emission loop compares the observed call to the complemented panel value; emission_total therefore counts complement-matches (5), and agreement_rate = emission_total / total_units yields 5/24 instead of the supplied-coding 19/24, while the derived quantity staged_agreement_units = total_units - emission_total back-computes the supplied-coding count for one narrative line, masking the inversion.", "issue_class": "issue-class:complemented-panel-for-supplied-panel-emission", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "panel_state complements the staged panel value before comparison: it returns PANEL_CODE_TOP (1) minus the staged panel_allele, and this complemented value is what the emission loop feeds into concordance_credit.", "observed_value": "panel value entering the emission = 1 - staged panel_allele", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 11, "quoted_text": "PANEL_CODE_TOP = 1"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 26, "end_line": 28, "quoted_text": "def panel_state(entry):\n    staged_value = int(entry[PANEL_COLUMN])\n    return PANEL_CODE_TOP - staged_value"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 39, "end_line": 41, "quoted_text": "emission_total = 0\nfor entry in rows:\n    emission_total = emission_total + concordance_credit(observed_state(entry), panel_state(entry))"}]}, {"description": "The reported selected-result agreement rate is 0.208333 (5/24) with emission 5.000 credits. Independent recount from inputs/data.csv shows pcr_call equals panel_allele as supplied for 19 of 24 isolates (mismatches only at ISO-004, ISO-007, ISO-013, ISO-018, ISO-023); 5/24 is exactly the agreement rate against the complemented panel.", "observed_value": "reported rate 5/24 = complement agreement; supplied-coding agreement is 19/24", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 17, "quoted_text": "Per-unit agreement rate used in the emission accumulation: 0.208333 (5/24)\nAccumulated concordance emission: 5.000 credits"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 21, "end_line": 21, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Observed-versus-panel concordance across 24 measured isolates: per-unit agreement rate 0.208333 (5/24), for an accumulated concordance emission of 5.000 credits."}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "ISO-004,Ward-B,2023,0.49,33.2,0,1"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "ISO-007,Ward-B,2024,0.60,26.6,1,0"}]}, {"description": "The governing task and the report's own scope statement both require the panel values in the coding in which they are supplied, so the complemented-panel emission is a deviation, and the report internally contradicts itself (19 staged-agreement units on one line versus a 5/24 rate two lines later).", "observed_value": "task requires supplied coding; report claims supplied coding but emits the complemented-panel rate", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one per-unit agreement rate for the emission-weighted comparison of the observed calls against the reference-panel values supplied with this workflow, using those panel values in the coding in which they are supplied."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "The analysis uses the supplied reference panel in the coding in which it is supplied."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "Units whose pcr_call equals the panel_allele as staged in inputs/data.csv: 19"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report does state the correct supplied-coding agreement count (19), which could suggest the supplied panel was used; however, tracing the code shows this number is staged_agreement_units = total_units - emission_total, a back-computed complement of the complemented-panel tally, and it does not feed the reported agreement rate, the emission credits, or the selected result, all of which carry the complement-derived 5/24 and 5.000.", "observed_value": "staged_agreement_units = 24 - 5 = 19 is derived from, not independent of, the complemented-panel emission, and is excluded from the selected result", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 43, "end_line": 45, "quoted_text": "staged_agreement_units = total_units - emission_total\nagreement_rate = emission_total / total_units\nagreement_fraction = fractions.Fraction(emission_total, total_units)"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "Units whose pcr_call equals the panel_allele as staged in inputs/data.csv: 19"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to defeat the verdict two ways. First, I considered whether PANEL_CODE_TOP - staged_value could be a legitimate coding normalization (e.g., if the panel were supplied in inverted coding); the report itself states panel_allele is supplied as 0/1 with the same semantics as pcr_call, the task mandates using the supplied coding, and no protocol deviation is claimed ('No protocol amendment or approved method deviation exists'), so the subtraction is a complementation, not a normalization. Second, I checked whether the selected result might nonetheless reflect the supplied-coding comparison: hand-recounting the 24 rows gives 19/24 agreement as supplied and 5/24 against the complement; the reported rate 0.208333 (5/24) and emission 5.000 match the complement exactly and cannot arise from the supplied coding. Both falsification attempts failed, so the demonstrated-issue verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}